==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Very good range.
* Fast moves with minimal endlag.
* Good [[Combos|combo]] potential.
* Good damage.
* Both moves can hit multiple targets.
* All moves can hit [[Sea Beast]]s.

|'''[Z] True Quiet Rush'''
* Reach extends further than its visuals.
* Decent mobility.

|'''[X] Focus Shot'''
* Very long range.
* Fast projectile and cast speed.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Small hitboxes.
* Hard to hit.
* Does not [[Instinct Break|break Instinct]].
* Attacks can require skills.

|'''[Z] True Quiet Rush'''
* Short range.

|'''[X] Focus Shot'''
* Predictable, which makes them very hard to hit a victim from afar.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Although Shizu is considered out meta by the community because of its bad hitbox and does not [[break Instinct]], its combos are still extremely fast and the sword itself deals good damage.
* Shizu, along with [[Oroshi]] and [[Saishi]] are required (and with 300 mastery on each respectively) to obtain the [[True Triple Katana]].
* Shizu is much like [[Canvander]] or [[Koko]].
** Many people refer to Shizu as an improved version of [[Cutlass]] and [[Katana]].
